1
00:00:32,470 --> 00:00:39,477
FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

2
00:02:11,611 --> 00:02:16,532
FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

3
00:02:16,616 --> 00:02:22,413
2016

4
00:02:22,997 --> 00:02:24,791
EPISODE 2

5
00:02:35,009 --> 00:02:36,511
I reserved this room.

6
00:02:38,846 --> 00:02:39,681
Oh, really?

7
00:02:43,768 --> 00:02:44,602
Sorry.

8
00:02:55,446 --> 00:02:56,322
You're here early.

9
00:03:00,285 --> 00:03:02,328
Weren't you coming
to the practice room today?

10
00:03:07,750 --> 00:03:10,670
Hey, you really don't remember me?

11
00:03:13,715 --> 00:03:16,759
We met at a competition
when we were kids and had fun.

12
00:03:17,260 --> 00:03:18,136
I don't remember.

13
00:03:19,220 --> 00:03:20,096
Seriously?

14
00:03:20,596 --> 00:03:22,682
Come on, think carefully.

15
00:03:22,765 --> 00:03:25,476
You lent me your handkerchief
when I asked.

16
00:03:26,102 --> 00:03:28,730
And when we played four hands,
we clicked so well that--

17
00:03:28,813 --> 00:03:31,065
I said I don't remember, so cut it out.

18
00:03:31,858 --> 00:03:33,234
I told you yesterday.

19
00:03:33,318 --> 00:03:35,528
I can't stand people
acting friendly with me.

20
00:03:41,576 --> 00:03:44,329
What's his problem?
Why did he get so worked up?

21
00:03:45,747 --> 00:03:47,081
2026 4TH QUARTER PRACTICAL LESSON FEES

22
00:03:51,044 --> 00:03:51,919
What?

23
00:03:52,503 --> 00:03:53,796
These are the practical lesson fees?

24
00:03:53,880 --> 00:03:56,382
How many zeros is that?
Four, five, six…

25
00:03:56,466 --> 00:03:57,842
Two million and…

26
00:03:57,925 --> 00:03:59,177
It's over two million won?

27
00:04:00,928 --> 00:04:02,513
Don't overthink it.

28
00:04:04,140 --> 00:04:05,725
It's a scholarship for being gifted.

29
00:04:05,808 --> 00:04:07,810
Why do you feel so pressured?

30
00:04:07,894 --> 00:04:10,772
I had no idea it'd be so expensive.

31
00:04:11,356 --> 00:04:12,190
Hey.

32
00:04:13,608 --> 00:04:14,859
Our school foundation

33
00:04:16,027 --> 00:04:17,487
has a ton of money.

34
00:04:18,905 --> 00:04:21,157
Besides, this isn't free.

35
00:04:22,033 --> 00:04:23,659
It's a win-win

36
00:04:24,243 --> 00:04:26,871
for both you and the school
when you become famous later.

37
00:04:29,457 --> 00:04:31,834
I just want to graduate high school.

38
00:04:34,045 --> 00:04:35,880
Why don't you have any ambition?

39
00:04:36,964 --> 00:04:38,925
You have a talent others would die for.

40
00:04:44,722 --> 00:04:45,765
Pay up first.

41
00:04:47,308 --> 00:04:48,976
You're relentless.

42
00:05:01,030 --> 00:05:02,407
I'm sorry.

43
00:05:02,490 --> 00:05:06,119
Professor Seo says he can't step out
because he's busy teaching.

44
00:05:06,619 --> 00:05:07,453
I'm really sorry.

45
00:05:14,585 --> 00:05:16,921
We even had a meeting a few days ago

46
00:05:17,004 --> 00:05:18,965
because both orchestras
wanted him so badly.

47
00:05:19,465 --> 00:05:22,051
But when I called today,
they'd both changed their minds.

48
00:05:22,760 --> 00:05:24,595
When I kept pressing them,

49
00:05:24,679 --> 00:05:26,389
they finally admitted

50
00:05:26,472 --> 00:05:29,767
Professor Seo demanded
that they choose either him or Pi-o.

51
00:05:30,435 --> 00:05:32,437
Can you believe that man?

52
00:05:32,520 --> 00:05:34,564
That's his own student.

53
00:05:35,148 --> 00:05:38,151
Is he trying to ruin Pi-o's career
because he acted out a bit?

54
00:06:00,715 --> 00:06:02,091
How are you going to fix this?

55
00:06:03,009 --> 00:06:04,969
Do you have any idea what you've done?

56
00:06:06,429 --> 00:06:08,931
Why did you challenge Professor Seo
without thinking it through?

57
00:06:16,314 --> 00:06:17,732
So what do you want me to do?

58
00:06:22,028 --> 00:06:23,154
Just go study abroad.

59
00:06:24,155 --> 00:06:25,781
You think this is a joke?

60
00:06:26,365 --> 00:06:29,243
Professor Seo told everyone
not to give you lessons,

61
00:06:29,327 --> 00:06:31,454
so there's no way
to get you a new teacher.

62
00:06:31,537 --> 00:06:33,039
Even the concerto fell through.

63
00:06:33,831 --> 00:06:35,333
We worked so hard to get here.

64
00:06:35,416 --> 00:06:37,418
How could you ruin everything overnight?

65
00:06:39,587 --> 00:06:40,922
You're better off studying abroad.

66
00:06:42,048 --> 00:06:45,051
You can't make it here,
and you would've studied abroad anyway.

67
00:06:45,927 --> 00:06:47,678
Just think of it as going a bit early.

68
00:06:47,762 --> 00:06:48,888
I already told you.

69
00:06:49,972 --> 00:06:52,350
I'm not going anywhere
until I get Grandfather's approval.

70
00:06:54,268 --> 00:06:56,896
You think I'd run off
to study abroad like a coward?

71
00:06:58,856 --> 00:06:59,857
Pi-o.

72
00:07:00,566 --> 00:07:01,692
Kang Pi-o!

73
00:07:10,451 --> 00:07:11,786
So?

74
00:07:11,869 --> 00:07:13,120
Are you happy now?

75
00:07:13,871 --> 00:07:16,499
What did you say
to get under his skin like that?

76
00:07:16,582 --> 00:07:19,335
Is your goal to make him
quit the piano by any means?

77
00:07:20,962 --> 00:07:21,921
Father!

78
00:07:47,613 --> 00:07:48,489
Welcome.

79
00:07:59,750 --> 00:08:01,002
Where are you going at this hour?

80
00:08:02,044 --> 00:08:03,921
-Heading to school?
-What do you care?

81
00:08:04,505 --> 00:08:06,048
Jeez, you're prickly.

82
00:08:06,132 --> 00:08:07,300
What did I ever do to you?

83
00:08:09,051 --> 00:08:09,969
You want the receipt?

84
00:08:12,430 --> 00:08:13,306
Huh?

85
00:08:30,531 --> 00:08:31,490
Welcome.

86
00:08:33,242 --> 00:08:35,244
Huh? What's this?

87
00:08:35,328 --> 00:08:36,621
Why is he here?

88
00:08:36,704 --> 00:08:38,039
Wait, is he one of those?

89
00:08:38,664 --> 00:08:39,665
An equity-based admit?

90
00:08:40,166 --> 00:08:41,626
Oh, right.

91
00:08:44,337 --> 00:08:47,548
That's more annoying
than buying your way in with donations.

92
00:08:52,094 --> 00:08:53,304
Jeez.

93
00:08:57,516 --> 00:08:58,726
Itadakimasu.

94
00:09:00,019 --> 00:09:02,271
We don't sell alcohol to minors.

95
00:09:02,355 --> 00:09:04,357
Whatever, you punk.

96
00:09:05,191 --> 00:09:06,734
Save it and ring this up.

97
00:09:07,443 --> 00:09:08,861
Don't you understand Korean?

98
00:09:09,362 --> 00:09:10,988
We don't sell alcohol to minors.

99
00:09:12,490 --> 00:09:15,660
Look, we get that you work hard,
but just ring us up already.

100
00:09:15,743 --> 00:09:17,286
You want a hard time at school?

101
00:09:17,370 --> 00:09:20,373
No, but if you're going to act like this,
respectfully get the hell out.

102
00:09:21,582 --> 00:09:22,458
Why you…

103
00:09:23,334 --> 00:09:25,044
Be a good charity case
and know your place.

104
00:09:25,127 --> 00:09:26,587
Who do you think you are?

105
00:09:26,671 --> 00:09:27,546
Hey.

106
00:09:28,547 --> 00:09:29,840
Stop trying to look tough

107
00:09:29,924 --> 00:09:31,300
and just hit me already.

108
00:09:31,384 --> 00:09:33,010
I'll gladly take
the easy settlement money.

109
00:09:34,303 --> 00:09:35,137
Hit me.

110
00:09:38,224 --> 00:09:39,058
Okay.

111
00:09:40,393 --> 00:09:41,227
Okay.

112
00:09:42,728 --> 00:09:43,688
This is enough, right?

113
00:09:50,736 --> 00:09:52,738
Man, the bag ripped open.

114
00:09:53,948 --> 00:09:55,783
Oh no, my hand slipped.

115
00:09:57,326 --> 00:09:58,285
-Sweet.
-Damn it.

116
00:09:59,370 --> 00:10:01,539
You might as well clean the whole place.

117
00:10:08,087 --> 00:10:09,213
Those bastards…

118
00:10:09,922 --> 00:10:11,257
Hey, who were those guys on camera?

119
00:10:11,966 --> 00:10:13,801
Look at this mess!

120
00:10:14,427 --> 00:10:18,556
What were you doing
while the store was getting trashed?

121
00:10:19,306 --> 00:10:21,308
-I'm sorry.
-Damn it.

122
00:10:22,393 --> 00:10:24,437
Who the hell were those bastards?

123
00:10:25,229 --> 00:10:27,440
Right, where's your parental consent form?

124
00:10:29,024 --> 00:10:29,900
The thing is…

125
00:10:31,944 --> 00:10:34,488
my parents aren't around.

126
00:10:35,072 --> 00:10:36,949
Get out of here, you punk!

127
00:10:37,575 --> 00:10:39,493
Sir, I'm really sorry.

128
00:10:41,620 --> 00:10:42,913
Damn it.

129
00:10:42,997 --> 00:10:43,831
Sir…

130
00:10:53,174 --> 00:10:54,258
Damn it.

131
00:10:56,010 --> 00:10:57,720
-Let's get you in.
-What took you so long?

132
00:10:58,929 --> 00:11:00,222
It's freezing out here.

133
00:11:01,891 --> 00:11:02,808
Let's go.

134
00:11:15,154 --> 00:11:17,198
KOREA ARTS HIGH SCHOOL
NAGWON MUSICAL INSTRUMENT ARCADE

135
00:12:25,599 --> 00:12:28,894
CHOI JEONG-YO

136
00:12:34,984 --> 00:12:36,402
I'm sure the composer

137
00:12:36,485 --> 00:12:39,321
wrote this piece to comfort someone.

138
00:12:39,864 --> 00:12:42,950
So instead of focusing on the notes,

139
00:12:43,033 --> 00:12:45,744
think about the emotions
the composer wanted to convey

140
00:12:45,828 --> 00:12:47,746
as you play, okay?

141
00:12:55,254 --> 00:12:57,756
LIKE SOOTHING A WOUNDED HEART

142
00:13:25,075 --> 00:13:26,410
CHOI JEONG-YO

143
00:13:39,131 --> 00:13:40,257
That arrogant jerk.

144
00:13:41,050 --> 00:13:42,843
Hey, Jerk Number Two is here.

145
00:14:01,362 --> 00:14:03,739
Hey, what's this now?

146
00:14:03,822 --> 00:14:06,033
He really must be a charity case.

147
00:14:06,116 --> 00:14:07,952
You're using copies
because you can't afford sheet music?

148
00:14:09,578 --> 00:14:11,163
-Give it back.
-I don't think so.

149
00:14:12,373 --> 00:14:14,333
Come and get it if you can.

150
00:14:14,416 --> 00:14:15,751
Give it back!

151
00:14:15,834 --> 00:14:17,586
What's the matter with them?

152
00:14:17,670 --> 00:14:20,756
This is why
you shouldn't have pissed me off!

153
00:14:20,839 --> 00:14:22,508
-Don't do it!
-Shit.

154
00:14:40,025 --> 00:14:41,652
Do you realize what that sheet music was?

155
00:14:43,904 --> 00:14:44,947
You crazy bastard!

156
00:14:46,657 --> 00:14:48,450
-Stop them.
-What do we do?

157
00:14:50,661 --> 00:14:51,495
Shit.

158
00:14:58,544 --> 00:14:59,795
-You bastard!
-Someone stop him!

159
00:15:04,842 --> 00:15:06,468
Come on, someone stop him!

160
00:15:19,773 --> 00:15:20,983
Will he face disciplinary action?

161
00:15:21,066 --> 00:15:22,151
Pi-o.

162
00:15:22,234 --> 00:15:23,277
Pi-o!

163
00:15:24,570 --> 00:15:27,156
Is it true Choi Jeong-yo
is facing a disciplinary hearing?

164
00:15:27,239 --> 00:15:28,115
Yeah.

165
00:15:28,615 --> 00:15:30,367
Oh no.

166
00:15:30,451 --> 00:15:32,828
What if he ends up getting disciplined?

167
00:15:33,495 --> 00:15:35,330
Anyone who uses violence
deserves punishment.

168
00:15:35,414 --> 00:15:37,249
Hey, how could you say that?

169
00:15:37,833 --> 00:15:39,752
Those two started it, didn't they?

170
00:15:40,252 --> 00:15:42,588
It's not the first time
those jerks have played dirty.

171
00:15:46,008 --> 00:15:47,009
Damn it.

172
00:15:47,092 --> 00:15:48,343
Hey, Pi-o!

173
00:15:48,427 --> 00:15:49,470
Where are you going?

174
00:15:58,812 --> 00:16:01,356
LIKE SOOTHING A WOUNDED HEART

175
00:16:05,194 --> 00:16:07,237
Do you realize what that sheet music was?

176
00:16:18,540 --> 00:16:19,917
Who the hell are you?

177
00:16:20,876 --> 00:16:22,211
Are you a thug or something?

178
00:16:22,294 --> 00:16:26,215
Just how low do you have to be
to mess up our boys' faces like that?

179
00:16:26,799 --> 00:16:27,841
Now what?

180
00:16:28,967 --> 00:16:30,177
What are you going to do about it?

181
00:16:30,260 --> 00:16:31,428
I'm very sorry.

182
00:16:32,304 --> 00:16:35,015
The school will pay
for both students' hospital bills.

183
00:16:35,099 --> 00:16:37,267
He's the one who caused trouble.

184
00:16:37,351 --> 00:16:39,978
So why is the school
paying the hospital bills?

185
00:16:41,105 --> 00:16:42,523
-Well…
-Besides,

186
00:16:42,606 --> 00:16:44,817
why aren't his parents here?

187
00:16:44,900 --> 00:16:45,776
As his teacher,

188
00:16:45,859 --> 00:16:48,445
I'm here in their place,
so you can speak with me.

189
00:16:48,529 --> 00:16:49,363
I'll ask again.

190
00:16:49,947 --> 00:16:52,407
Why is his teacher here
instead of his parents?

191
00:16:52,491 --> 00:16:55,369
I don't have any parents,
so just talk to me.

192
00:16:57,830 --> 00:16:59,123
No wonder.

193
00:16:59,206 --> 00:17:01,792
I could tell
you didn't have a proper upbringing.

194
00:17:03,627 --> 00:17:04,920
What about Jang Seok-hwan?

195
00:17:05,963 --> 00:17:08,799
You think it looks like
he had a good upbringing?

196
00:17:08,882 --> 00:17:10,384
-Jeong-yo!
-What did you say?

197
00:17:11,426 --> 00:17:12,719
You uneducated bastard.

198
00:17:12,803 --> 00:17:14,388
-You little punk.
-Ma'am.

199
00:17:14,471 --> 00:17:16,306
-You dare badmouth Seok-hwan?
-Please calm down.

200
00:17:20,769 --> 00:17:22,980
I'll mess up your face too, you punk.

201
00:17:23,063 --> 00:17:24,356
Please take a seat, ma'am.

202
00:17:43,709 --> 00:17:45,002
I just have one question.

203
00:17:45,627 --> 00:17:48,046
How did a student with no parents

204
00:17:48,130 --> 00:17:49,756
get transferred to this school?

205
00:17:49,840 --> 00:17:52,050
He was selected as a gifted scholar.

206
00:17:52,134 --> 00:17:53,552
"Gifted"?

207
00:17:53,635 --> 00:17:54,678
Yes.

208
00:17:56,722 --> 00:18:01,727
Just how talented is he
that he can be so ill-mannered

209
00:18:02,311 --> 00:18:04,354
and still earn a scholarship?

210
00:18:05,689 --> 00:18:07,357
Was he even chosen fairly?

211
00:18:07,441 --> 00:18:09,776
Whatever, I don't care.

212
00:18:11,069 --> 00:18:13,906
I refuse to forgive him,

213
00:18:14,406 --> 00:18:15,449
so have him expelled.

214
00:18:17,826 --> 00:18:18,744
I understand.

215
00:18:19,745 --> 00:18:21,038
I'll have him expelled.

216
00:18:21,121 --> 00:18:22,289
Ma'am!

217
00:18:22,372 --> 00:18:24,708
Given that the two students
were badly hurt,

218
00:18:24,791 --> 00:18:27,336
I'm afraid
Choi Jeong-yo will be held accountable.

219
00:18:28,045 --> 00:18:29,963
We'll take the proper action,
so don't worry.

220
00:18:41,099 --> 00:18:41,975
Seon-ju.

221
00:18:42,059 --> 00:18:45,354
They were the ones who picked a fight,
so why is Jeong-yo getting expelled?

222
00:18:45,437 --> 00:18:48,982
And why bother transferring him here
just to expel him over something so minor?

223
00:18:49,066 --> 00:18:51,610
If he's a lost cause,
it's better to cut him loose.

224
00:18:52,236 --> 00:18:54,029
You've seen brilliant pianists quit

225
00:18:54,112 --> 00:18:56,865
because their personal lives were a mess.

226
00:18:58,200 --> 00:19:00,702
This is a school, and I'm the director.

227
00:19:05,874 --> 00:19:09,294
This is a school matter now,
so back off from Choi Jeong-yo.

228
00:19:10,379 --> 00:19:11,296
Seon-ju!

229
00:19:14,967 --> 00:19:16,635
I'll just leave, Mr. Do.

230
00:19:16,718 --> 00:19:19,471
What are you talking about, Jeong-yo?

231
00:19:19,554 --> 00:19:23,600
I'll make sure
you don't get expelled, so just…

232
00:19:23,684 --> 00:19:24,643
No, it's okay.

233
00:19:25,310 --> 00:19:26,645
I don't think…

234
00:19:28,897 --> 00:19:30,732
I belong here anyway.

235
00:19:31,900 --> 00:19:32,985
This is for the best.

236
00:19:34,903 --> 00:19:36,488
Thank you for everything you've done.

237
00:19:43,745 --> 00:19:44,663
Jeong-yo.

238
00:20:10,105 --> 00:20:13,233
LIKE SOOTHING A WOUNDED HEART

239
00:20:44,723 --> 00:20:45,640
Where are you going?

240
00:20:47,809 --> 00:20:49,061
It was nice meeting you.

241
00:20:49,978 --> 00:20:50,979
Have a good life.

242
00:21:18,715 --> 00:21:19,549
Jeong-yo!

243
00:21:21,426 --> 00:21:22,344
Choi Jeong-yo!

244
00:21:39,694 --> 00:21:42,030
Where did you get this footage?

245
00:21:42,114 --> 00:21:45,033
Is that so important right now?

246
00:21:48,161 --> 00:21:50,956
I'm not defending Choi Jeong-yo's actions.

247
00:21:52,749 --> 00:21:56,336
But taking advantage of a part-time worker
who can't defend himself

248
00:21:56,837 --> 00:21:59,172
will spark public outrage.

249
00:22:00,632 --> 00:22:01,842
If you refuse to settle,

250
00:22:02,467 --> 00:22:04,928
we'll have to make this footage public.

251
00:22:05,929 --> 00:22:08,098
And you'll need to think carefully about

252
00:22:08,598 --> 00:22:10,767
who will suffer from that.

253
00:22:18,233 --> 00:22:20,861
Let's each compromise a bit, shall we?

254
00:22:31,997 --> 00:22:34,499
Mr. Do, isn't it better if I just leave?

255
00:22:39,921 --> 00:22:41,673
If you hate feeling like you owe us,

256
00:22:42,257 --> 00:22:44,384
then become a great musician.

257
00:22:48,013 --> 00:22:50,765
If you leave now,
it puts us in a tight spot too.

258
00:23:02,861 --> 00:23:05,238
ORIGINAL DECISION: EXPULSION
REVIEW RESULTS: EXPULSION OVERTURNED

259
00:23:05,322 --> 00:23:06,531
REASON FOR REVIEW: NEW FINDINGS

260
00:23:15,624 --> 00:23:16,625
That's impossible.

261
00:23:17,501 --> 00:23:19,794
Why are you saying it's impossible
without even trying?

262
00:23:20,712 --> 00:23:22,172
He's incredibly talented,

263
00:23:23,340 --> 00:23:27,135
but he lacks the basics
from playing however he wanted.

264
00:23:27,886 --> 00:23:29,471
He hasn't adjusted to school yet,

265
00:23:30,138 --> 00:23:31,723
so I don't think we should push him.

266
00:23:31,806 --> 00:23:33,558
Hyun-soo, my pride is at stake.

267
00:23:36,603 --> 00:23:37,521
Also,

268
00:23:38,855 --> 00:23:40,482
if we don't prove his talent,

269
00:23:40,565 --> 00:23:44,069
those people will jump at any chance
to get Jeong-yo kicked out again.

270
00:23:45,654 --> 00:23:46,613
You must bring me

271
00:23:47,239 --> 00:23:49,491
tangible results within a month.

272
00:23:50,742 --> 00:23:53,286
It's the only way to protect
both Jeong-yo and us.

273
00:24:08,718 --> 00:24:10,011
Hi, Hyun-soo.

274
00:24:19,354 --> 00:24:20,272
These days,

275
00:24:21,189 --> 00:24:23,316
kids are so open when it comes to dating.

276
00:24:25,110 --> 00:24:27,946
We could never be that open
back in our day, right?

277
00:24:32,617 --> 00:24:34,202
It reminds me of high school.

278
00:24:36,246 --> 00:24:38,164
I couldn't make my feelings obvious

279
00:24:39,040 --> 00:24:40,959
and just worried about the competition.

280
00:24:48,383 --> 00:24:50,302
Why did you come see me today?

281
00:24:50,385 --> 00:24:52,512
It can't be to reminisce
about the good old days.

282
00:24:53,763 --> 00:24:54,723
Hyun-soo.

283
00:24:55,849 --> 00:24:57,475
Take Pi-o under your wing.

284
00:24:59,060 --> 00:25:01,396
I know you don't want to.

285
00:25:01,980 --> 00:25:04,107
It's awkward for me to ask this too.

286
00:25:05,442 --> 00:25:07,986
But Pi-o refuses anyone but you,
so what choice do I have?

287
00:25:08,987 --> 00:25:10,655
Don't read too much into it.

288
00:25:11,239 --> 00:25:12,741
For old times' sake,

289
00:25:13,700 --> 00:25:15,619
can't you just take him on?

290
00:25:26,212 --> 00:25:27,297
-Feel the butterflies?
-Are you serious?

291
00:26:00,330 --> 00:26:02,248
-No way!
-But he's cute.

292
00:26:02,332 --> 00:26:03,667
-What?
-Really?

293
00:26:06,920 --> 00:26:07,921
Seriously.

294
00:26:09,172 --> 00:26:10,632
Why is it so loud here?

295
00:26:23,395 --> 00:26:25,689
Do you still want to take lessons from me?

296
00:26:46,376 --> 00:26:47,544
Four hands?

297
00:26:48,128 --> 00:26:49,295
Yes.

298
00:26:49,379 --> 00:26:51,631
I'll decide whether to teach you
based on that.

299
00:26:52,257 --> 00:26:53,925
I need to be sure of you too.

300
00:26:54,008 --> 00:26:56,636
But why does it have to be four hands?

301
00:26:56,720 --> 00:27:00,348
I barely have enough time
to learn my solo repertoire.

302
00:27:00,432 --> 00:27:01,808
Wrong.

303
00:27:01,891 --> 00:27:04,394
That mindset alone
shows how impatient you are.

304
00:27:06,020 --> 00:27:07,522
You think you lack skills?

305
00:27:08,356 --> 00:27:09,190
That's not true.

306
00:27:10,608 --> 00:27:13,319
What you need most right now

307
00:27:13,403 --> 00:27:14,946
is emotional connection.

308
00:27:15,029 --> 00:27:18,783
And playing four hands
is the best way to feel that.

309
00:27:19,868 --> 00:27:21,995
Can I at least choose my partner?

310
00:27:22,078 --> 00:27:24,289
No, I already have someone in mind.

311
00:27:24,372 --> 00:27:25,749
I'm sure you know Choi Jeong-yo.

312
00:27:25,832 --> 00:27:27,000
The new transfer student.

313
00:27:28,126 --> 00:27:29,878
The way I see it, you…

314
00:27:29,961 --> 00:27:31,671
Why him, of all people?

315
00:27:32,255 --> 00:27:34,966
He's never even had any proper lessons.

316
00:27:41,931 --> 00:27:43,558
Have you listened to him play?

317
00:27:45,685 --> 00:27:47,604
And you still don't know why I chose him?

318
00:27:50,398 --> 00:27:52,108
Or are you like the other kids

319
00:27:52,776 --> 00:27:54,611
and don't want to hang out
with a poor classmate?

320
00:27:54,694 --> 00:27:56,488
-It's not that, sir.
-Then what is it?

321
00:28:00,700 --> 00:28:03,536
Fine, let's stop here.
Forget about the lessons.

322
00:28:03,620 --> 00:28:05,872
I don't want to teach someone
who's being stubborn

323
00:28:06,581 --> 00:28:07,749
from day one.

324
00:28:09,417 --> 00:28:11,252
I'll do it. Four hands.

325
00:28:15,215 --> 00:28:16,633
I'll play four hands…

326
00:28:19,719 --> 00:28:20,804
with Choi Jeong-yo.

327
00:28:34,567 --> 00:28:35,485
Thank you.

328
00:28:39,614 --> 00:28:41,032
I asked to see you

329
00:28:41,115 --> 00:28:43,409
about playing
at next month's progress recital.

330
00:28:43,493 --> 00:28:44,619
Progress recital?

331
00:28:44,702 --> 00:28:45,995
What's that?

332
00:28:46,079 --> 00:28:49,082
It's a monthly performance
held at the school's art center.

333
00:28:51,918 --> 00:28:53,962
To put this incident behind us,

334
00:28:54,045 --> 00:28:56,047
you need to show what you're capable of.

335
00:28:56,130 --> 00:28:57,966
But it'll be hard to do on your own,

336
00:28:58,049 --> 00:28:59,968
so how about playing four hands?

337
00:29:00,051 --> 00:29:01,594
Hold on, Mr. Do.

338
00:29:06,724 --> 00:29:08,393
Are you telling me…

339
00:29:10,270 --> 00:29:12,438
that I need to perform?

340
00:29:12,522 --> 00:29:14,315
Why? What's the problem?

341
00:29:15,233 --> 00:29:17,902
Everyone at the school participates
in the progress recitals.

342
00:29:18,903 --> 00:29:19,904
But…

343
00:29:23,032 --> 00:29:25,326
I'm not too confident about performing.

344
00:29:25,910 --> 00:29:27,954
No musician feels confident performing.

345
00:29:28,037 --> 00:29:29,664
Everyone gets nervous.

346
00:29:31,875 --> 00:29:32,876
Still…

347
00:29:33,668 --> 00:29:36,379
For now, don't argue with me

348
00:29:37,839 --> 00:29:38,882
and give it a try.

349
00:29:40,967 --> 00:29:41,968
But sir…

350
00:29:44,137 --> 00:29:46,014
Tomorrow at 6 p.m.
in the small auditorium.

351
00:29:46,806 --> 00:29:48,975
I'll text you my pick for the piece.

352
00:29:49,934 --> 00:29:51,269
Send me yours if you have any.

353
00:29:52,020 --> 00:29:53,354
Wait a minute.

354
00:29:54,689 --> 00:29:57,984
We're supposed to be partners.
Shouldn't we talk things through?

355
00:29:58,568 --> 00:30:00,069
Why are you being so combative?

356
00:30:02,488 --> 00:30:04,741
Does it look like I want to do this?

357
00:30:45,823 --> 00:30:47,116
Do you have any idea what time it is?

358
00:30:49,911 --> 00:30:50,787
What?

359
00:30:54,165 --> 00:30:55,500
Am I that late?

360
00:30:55,583 --> 00:30:57,126
Sorry, I had to eat before coming.

361
00:30:57,210 --> 00:31:00,213
You should've let me know.
Why didn't you text me?

362
00:31:01,130 --> 00:31:04,384
My phone is old,
so the battery keeps dying.

363
00:31:04,467 --> 00:31:06,052
It drives me crazy too.

364
00:31:07,679 --> 00:31:08,554
Let's get started.

365
00:31:12,475 --> 00:31:16,020
Hey, why are you always so impatient?

366
00:31:16,521 --> 00:31:19,399
I just ate. Give me some time to digest.

367
00:31:19,482 --> 00:31:21,567
Stop talking nonsense and sit down.

368
00:31:36,666 --> 00:31:37,542
Hold on.

369
00:31:37,625 --> 00:31:40,378
I feel so sick all of a sudden.

370
00:31:41,004 --> 00:31:42,630
Did that food give me indigestion?

371
00:31:43,297 --> 00:31:44,799
What are you playing at?

372
00:31:47,093 --> 00:31:49,554
Hey, I don't think I can do this today.

373
00:31:49,637 --> 00:31:51,097
Let's practice tomorrow. I'm sorry.

374
00:31:51,180 --> 00:31:52,849
Hey. Hey!

375
00:31:55,143 --> 00:31:56,436
Damn it.

376
00:32:05,069 --> 00:32:05,945
Oh jeez.

377
00:32:12,994 --> 00:32:16,581
In classical poetry,
Goryeo songs have a three-beat rhythm.

378
00:32:17,165 --> 00:32:19,292
That's why they feature repeated refrains

379
00:32:19,375 --> 00:32:21,961
and expressions drawn from
everyday, colloquial language.

380
00:32:22,920 --> 00:32:26,007
If a poem with a three-beat rhythm
appears on the exam,

381
00:32:26,090 --> 00:32:27,467
you can assume it's a Goryeo song.

382
00:32:32,847 --> 00:32:34,223
Hey.

383
00:32:34,307 --> 00:32:36,142
You lied about being sick, didn't you?

384
00:32:36,809 --> 00:32:37,643
I know you did.

385
00:32:39,145 --> 00:32:40,605
I really was sick!

386
00:32:56,079 --> 00:32:58,414
I'm sick, so I can't make it again.

387
00:32:58,498 --> 00:32:59,707
Let's meet at 7 a.m. tomorrow.

388
00:33:00,583 --> 00:33:01,876
Are you kidding me?

389
00:33:13,387 --> 00:33:14,347
Are you just getting in?

390
00:33:15,556 --> 00:33:16,808
Have you eaten?

391
00:33:17,642 --> 00:33:18,476
Yes.

392
00:33:24,023 --> 00:33:25,817
How are things coming along?

393
00:33:25,900 --> 00:33:27,276
Hyun-soo told me

394
00:33:27,360 --> 00:33:29,278
that you're playing
four hands with Jeong-yo.

395
00:33:32,740 --> 00:33:36,244
I told you Hyun-soo agreed
to teach Pi-o, right?

396
00:33:36,327 --> 00:33:39,872
He's in good hands with Hyun-soo,
so that's a relief.

397
00:33:47,797 --> 00:33:50,758
Go upstairs and rest. You must be tired.

398
00:33:51,884 --> 00:33:52,802
Okay.

399
00:34:03,104 --> 00:34:04,772
I'll give you one more chance.

400
00:34:05,815 --> 00:34:07,984
If you're late again, I'll kill you.

401
00:34:22,623 --> 00:34:23,583
6:30 A.M.

402
00:34:41,184 --> 00:34:42,059
Hey, Choi Jeong-yo!

403
00:34:43,477 --> 00:34:44,687
What the heck?

404
00:34:44,770 --> 00:34:45,771
Hyun-chul!

405
00:34:46,981 --> 00:34:48,816
How did you know I was here?

406
00:34:48,900 --> 00:34:51,527
Min-su told me he saw you
wearing this school's uniform.

407
00:34:51,611 --> 00:34:53,529
Why haven't you answered my calls?

408
00:34:53,613 --> 00:34:54,947
Oh, sorry.

409
00:34:55,907 --> 00:34:58,451
And how did you transfer to this school?

410
00:34:58,534 --> 00:35:00,494
It just kind of happened.

411
00:35:01,329 --> 00:35:02,788
So what's going on?

412
00:35:04,165 --> 00:35:06,250
Let's go and talk somewhere else.

413
00:35:06,334 --> 00:35:08,502
What? But I have to go…

414
00:35:09,879 --> 00:35:10,796
Jeez.

415
00:35:11,797 --> 00:35:12,632
Damn it.

416
00:35:43,162 --> 00:35:45,665
I stopped Min-su from running his mouth,

417
00:35:45,748 --> 00:35:47,208
but Kim is raising hell right now,

418
00:35:47,291 --> 00:35:49,835
demanding the kids tell him where you are.

419
00:35:50,962 --> 00:35:52,129
Damn it.

420
00:35:52,213 --> 00:35:55,341
I came up with a story
saying you skipped town,

421
00:35:56,217 --> 00:35:59,470
but Kim is a persistent bastard,
and I'm worried about what he'll do.

422
00:36:00,012 --> 00:36:02,723
So keep a low profile and stay hidden.

423
00:36:02,807 --> 00:36:04,475
-Got it?
-Okay.

424
00:36:07,311 --> 00:36:08,562
So he doesn't know

425
00:36:09,689 --> 00:36:11,357
where my dad went?

426
00:36:12,108 --> 00:36:13,859
That's what you're worried about?

427
00:36:14,860 --> 00:36:16,696
What kind of parent
ditches their kid and bolts?

428
00:36:44,056 --> 00:36:44,932
Pi-o.

429
00:36:48,561 --> 00:36:49,478
I'm sorry.

430
00:36:50,730 --> 00:36:52,023
Something urgent came up.

431
00:36:58,654 --> 00:37:00,531
Want to practice during lunch break?

432
00:37:01,991 --> 00:37:03,242
How do you reserve a practice room?

433
00:37:04,035 --> 00:37:06,370
I'll reserve one this time.

434
00:37:07,121 --> 00:37:09,206
No, there's no need.

435
00:37:10,082 --> 00:37:11,042
Let's just drop it.

436
00:37:12,501 --> 00:37:14,211
Come on, don't be like that.

437
00:37:14,295 --> 00:37:16,672
Something came up, and I had no choice.

438
00:37:26,307 --> 00:37:28,851
I said I had no choice.

439
00:37:34,315 --> 00:37:35,858
You think playing the piano is a joke?

440
00:37:37,026 --> 00:37:39,403
I guess it's nothing more
than fun and games to you.

441
00:37:40,196 --> 00:37:41,197
But you know what?

442
00:37:42,490 --> 00:37:45,242
I hate bastards like you
who play music with that attitude.

443
00:37:48,913 --> 00:37:51,207
If you're going to act like that,
just quit school.

444
00:38:01,258 --> 00:38:03,677
That prickly little punk.

445
00:38:04,428 --> 00:38:07,640
Choi Jeong-yo? Screw him.

446
00:38:08,808 --> 00:38:09,934
Smash it more.

447
00:38:15,648 --> 00:38:18,442
KOREA ARTS HIGH SCHOOL

448
00:38:18,526 --> 00:38:19,985
-It'll be fine.
-Yeah, but…

449
00:38:20,069 --> 00:38:21,821
-He won't know.
-He won't?

450
00:38:21,904 --> 00:38:22,863
I just…

451
00:38:24,281 --> 00:38:25,241
What?

452
00:38:25,324 --> 00:38:27,493
Man, he's annoying.

453
00:38:41,715 --> 00:38:42,800
Hey.

454
00:38:43,676 --> 00:38:45,594
Damn it.

455
00:38:48,139 --> 00:38:48,973
Move.

456
00:38:55,438 --> 00:38:56,480
Wait.

457
00:38:56,564 --> 00:38:57,857
What are you doing?

458
00:39:04,780 --> 00:39:05,739
What is that?

459
00:39:05,823 --> 00:39:07,867
-Who did that?
-Damn it.

460
00:39:09,160 --> 00:39:10,035
Who would do that?

461
00:39:15,332 --> 00:39:17,168
Someone go get the teachers.

462
00:39:20,254 --> 00:39:22,840
Hey, it was his idea!

463
00:39:23,507 --> 00:39:24,675
You traitor!

464
00:39:24,758 --> 00:39:26,427
Hey, hold on!

465
00:39:27,887 --> 00:39:28,804
What are you doing?

466
00:39:28,888 --> 00:39:29,722
Shit!

467
00:39:29,805 --> 00:39:31,140
Wait!

468
00:39:31,223 --> 00:39:32,850
Wait! Stop!

469
00:39:32,933 --> 00:39:34,477
Stop!

470
00:39:34,560 --> 00:39:35,478
Hey.

471
00:39:37,313 --> 00:39:39,106
-Stop it.
-Let go!

472
00:39:39,190 --> 00:39:41,525
That bastard tried to ruin my hands!

473
00:39:42,651 --> 00:39:43,861
Are you insane?

474
00:39:43,944 --> 00:39:45,863
You'll only make things worse.

475
00:39:48,824 --> 00:39:49,658
Let me see.

476
00:39:52,244 --> 00:39:53,746
Damn it.

477
00:39:53,829 --> 00:39:54,830
Nurse's office. Now.

478
00:39:54,914 --> 00:39:56,499
What do you care?

479
00:39:57,917 --> 00:39:59,877
Stop being stubborn.

480
00:40:00,461 --> 00:40:02,129
What if the glass
digs deeper into your skin?

481
00:40:16,143 --> 00:40:16,977
I'll do it.

482
00:40:18,187 --> 00:40:19,230
Sure.

483
00:40:24,443 --> 00:40:25,277
Leave.

484
00:40:26,237 --> 00:40:27,488
I'll take care of the rest.

485
00:40:35,246 --> 00:40:36,956
Why aren't you leaving?

486
00:40:39,792 --> 00:40:41,126
I'm sorry about yesterday.

487
00:40:44,004 --> 00:40:45,005
Actually,

488
00:40:46,549 --> 00:40:48,425
there's something I haven't told you.

489
00:40:49,134 --> 00:40:51,512
What is it that you haven't told me?

490
00:40:52,429 --> 00:40:53,806
The truth is…

491
00:40:55,891 --> 00:40:57,977
At some point,
going on stage started to scare me.

492
00:41:00,062 --> 00:41:02,022
I'm fine when I play by myself,

493
00:41:03,899 --> 00:41:06,610
but thinking about the stage
makes me break out in a cold sweat,

494
00:41:06,694 --> 00:41:08,112
and I can't breathe.

495
00:41:09,071 --> 00:41:12,283
I think that's why I kept missing
or showing up late to practice.

496
00:41:13,742 --> 00:41:14,577
Why?

497
00:41:16,954 --> 00:41:17,955
Is it…

498
00:41:19,623 --> 00:41:21,000
because of what happened that day?

499
00:41:23,627 --> 00:41:24,753
Yeah.

500
00:41:27,756 --> 00:41:31,135
I tried to get over it, but it's not easy.

501
00:41:33,178 --> 00:41:35,681
I should've been honest from the start.

502
00:41:35,764 --> 00:41:36,807
I'm sorry.

503
00:41:45,274 --> 00:41:46,233
Oh, right.

504
00:41:47,693 --> 00:41:49,903
I'll make sure Mr. Do understands,

505
00:41:49,987 --> 00:41:51,196
so don't worry.

506
00:42:07,171 --> 00:42:08,422
The grand prize goes to

507
00:42:08,505 --> 00:42:10,591
Choi Jeong-yo!

508
00:42:14,178 --> 00:42:16,055
There's a medical emergency.

509
00:42:16,138 --> 00:42:17,556
Mom!

510
00:42:17,640 --> 00:42:20,142
-Mom!
-Ma'am?

511
00:42:20,225 --> 00:42:23,187
Mom! You're okay, right?

512
00:42:23,270 --> 00:42:24,104
Mom!

513
00:42:26,231 --> 00:42:27,316
Mom.

514
00:42:27,399 --> 00:42:30,444
Mom. Mom!

515
00:43:02,935 --> 00:43:05,854
Did you tell Mr. Do what we talked about?

516
00:43:07,231 --> 00:43:08,857
No. Why?

517
00:43:13,779 --> 00:43:15,572
Then don't tell him yet.

518
00:43:15,656 --> 00:43:17,658
Come to the small auditorium
tomorrow by 9 p.m.

519
00:43:35,634 --> 00:43:36,552
What's all this?

520
00:43:40,180 --> 00:43:42,641
I told you yesterday
that I can't get on stage--

521
00:43:42,725 --> 00:43:44,017
Just come in and sit down.

522
00:44:19,386 --> 00:44:20,763
If you're going to perform,

523
00:44:20,846 --> 00:44:22,806
you have to get used to the stage.

524
00:44:23,891 --> 00:44:26,310
If you start out playing
like you're not onstage

525
00:44:26,393 --> 00:44:28,020
and gradually increase the pressure,

526
00:44:29,146 --> 00:44:30,564
you'll be fine in no time.

527
00:44:36,737 --> 00:44:38,614
You're not the only one with stage fright.

528
00:44:40,616 --> 00:44:42,075
The degree may vary,

529
00:44:42,618 --> 00:44:45,788
but all performers experience it.

530
00:44:46,455 --> 00:44:48,624
You just have to face it and deal with it.

531
00:44:49,166 --> 00:44:51,168
Avoiding it won't do any good.

532
00:44:54,755 --> 00:44:55,672
So?

533
00:44:57,049 --> 00:44:58,091
Think you can do it?

534
00:45:03,806 --> 00:45:04,932
I'll give it a try.

535
00:48:02,150 --> 00:48:03,110
What time is it?

536
00:48:05,320 --> 00:48:06,196
It's 1 a.m.?

537
00:48:07,197 --> 00:48:08,156
It's 1 a.m.?

538
00:48:20,335 --> 00:48:21,253
Huh?

539
00:48:21,336 --> 00:48:23,463
Hey, why are all the lights turned off?

540
00:48:23,547 --> 00:48:24,381
The door!

541
00:48:25,215 --> 00:48:27,009
They lock the door at this hour?

542
00:48:32,305 --> 00:48:35,892
Why would they lock this up
with someone inside?

543
00:48:35,976 --> 00:48:38,895
They probably didn't think
anyone would be in the small auditorium.

544
00:48:47,487 --> 00:48:48,822
Who are you calling?

545
00:48:48,905 --> 00:48:50,907
We should at least tell
our homeroom teacher.

546
00:48:50,991 --> 00:48:51,825
Hey.

547
00:48:51,908 --> 00:48:53,827
I got into trouble not too long ago.

548
00:48:53,910 --> 00:48:55,954
What do you think they'll do to me
if they find out?

549
00:48:56,038 --> 00:48:57,414
What should we do then?

550
00:49:03,378 --> 00:49:04,713
Where are you going?

551
00:49:05,672 --> 00:49:06,631
Damn it.

552
00:49:08,425 --> 00:49:10,260
This is a good spot. Lots of leaves too.

553
00:49:11,636 --> 00:49:13,180
Don't tell me you want us to jump.

554
00:49:17,726 --> 00:49:18,894
Wait, Choi Jeong-yo.

555
00:49:21,938 --> 00:49:24,733
Hey, Choi Jeong-yo! Are you okay?

556
00:49:25,484 --> 00:49:26,818
Get down here already.

557
00:49:27,527 --> 00:49:29,321
You crazy bastard.

558
00:49:29,404 --> 00:49:30,363
Come on down.

559
00:49:32,699 --> 00:49:33,700
Hurry up!

560
00:49:57,224 --> 00:49:58,100
Let's go.

561
00:50:05,565 --> 00:50:06,858
That was fun, right?

562
00:50:06,942 --> 00:50:07,901
Whatever.

563
00:50:09,027 --> 00:50:12,072
KOREA ARTS HIGH SCHOOL

564
00:50:26,169 --> 00:50:28,672
I'm the king of the world!

565
00:50:40,142 --> 00:50:41,226
Hey, you punks!

566
00:50:42,018 --> 00:50:43,854
What do you think you're doing?

567
00:50:45,105 --> 00:50:47,274
-Hey, let's run.
-Okay.

568
00:50:48,066 --> 00:50:49,317
Stop right there!

569
00:50:50,193 --> 00:50:52,654
What class are you in?

570
00:51:17,137 --> 00:51:18,763
Can we practice tomorrow too?

571
00:51:22,058 --> 00:51:24,895
What's up with him? Why is he so eager?

572
00:51:29,983 --> 00:51:30,859
All right.

573
00:51:36,823 --> 00:51:37,949
All right.

574
00:51:38,033 --> 00:51:40,285
All right.

575
00:51:54,507 --> 00:51:55,759
What's wrong with you?

576
00:51:55,842 --> 00:51:56,801
Just open the door.

577
00:51:59,221 --> 00:52:00,180
Get inside.

578
00:52:00,805 --> 00:52:01,806
Hurry up.

579
00:52:25,080 --> 00:52:26,498
Let's go somewhere tomorrow.

580
00:52:29,834 --> 00:52:30,669
Where?

581
00:52:35,257 --> 00:52:36,549
You'll see when we get there.

582
00:52:44,766 --> 00:52:46,810
Come on, fill me in.

583
00:52:46,893 --> 00:52:48,353
Where are we going?

584
00:52:49,104 --> 00:52:50,397
You'll see when we get there.

585
00:52:52,190 --> 00:52:53,400
Jeez.

586
00:53:11,209 --> 00:53:12,252
What is this?

587
00:53:13,420 --> 00:53:15,380
You want us to perform here?

588
00:53:15,463 --> 00:53:18,008
We need to see if you can play
in front of an audience.

589
00:53:19,175 --> 00:53:20,010
Hey.

590
00:53:20,760 --> 00:53:22,887
I'm not ready to do this yet.

591
00:53:23,596 --> 00:53:25,140
I'm really sorry.

592
00:53:27,475 --> 00:53:29,519
Nobody here knows who you are.

593
00:53:29,602 --> 00:53:31,688
They don't care one bit about you.

594
00:53:31,771 --> 00:53:33,523
It'll be easier here than on a real stage.

595
00:53:33,606 --> 00:53:35,275
That's just your opinion!

596
00:53:36,776 --> 00:53:39,446
If it were that easy,
do you think I would've struggled so much?

597
00:53:40,989 --> 00:53:42,324
I can't do it.

598
00:53:42,407 --> 00:53:44,492
How long are you going to
keep playing in hiding?

599
00:53:45,201 --> 00:53:46,995
It's time to come out of your cave!

600
00:53:51,291 --> 00:53:53,168
I know this is hard for you.

601
00:53:53,251 --> 00:53:55,712
But ignoring the problem
won't solve anything.

602
00:53:56,546 --> 00:53:58,923
You need to face it at some point.

603
00:54:00,842 --> 00:54:02,344
If you can't look at the people,

604
00:54:03,094 --> 00:54:04,763
pretend we're practicing and look at me.

605
00:54:06,056 --> 00:54:07,640
Pretend there's no audience.

606
00:54:08,475 --> 00:54:09,768
Just focus on my playing.

607
00:54:52,602 --> 00:54:54,687
If you start out playing
like you're not on stage,

608
00:54:55,397 --> 00:54:58,274
then gradually increase the pressure,
you'll be fine in no time.

609
00:55:01,403 --> 00:55:03,238
You're not the only one with stage fright.

610
00:55:03,321 --> 00:55:05,949
All performers have it.

611
00:55:06,699 --> 00:55:08,743
You just have to face it and deal with it.

612
00:55:09,285 --> 00:55:11,287
Avoiding it won't do any good.

613
00:57:28,299 --> 00:57:32,053
The train approaching
is bound for Sinhadam.

614
00:57:32,136 --> 00:57:34,597
Please take a step back.

615
00:58:38,786 --> 00:58:40,913
FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

616
00:58:40,997 --> 00:58:42,915
You don't follow the sheet music.

617
00:58:42,999 --> 00:58:45,543
I think Chopin would say it's fine.

618
00:58:45,627 --> 00:58:47,211
Audition for the concerto.

619
00:58:47,295 --> 00:58:50,548
Didn't your grandfather tell you
he asked to see Choi Jeong-yo?

620
00:58:50,632 --> 00:58:52,592
I didn't play a duet with you
because I wanted to.

621
00:58:52,675 --> 00:58:54,969
One minute you're nice, then you're mad.
Make up your mind, damn it.

622
00:58:55,053 --> 00:58:56,012
What the hell is it then?

623
00:58:56,095 --> 00:58:57,930
-What's going on?
-Stop them! Hey!

624
00:58:59,891 --> 00:59:00,808
Mom.

625
00:59:02,685 --> 00:59:04,187
Don't think about anything.

626
00:59:04,270 --> 00:59:05,313
Just focus on my voice

627
00:59:05,938 --> 00:59:07,815
and my playing.

628
00:59:09,275 --> 00:59:14,280
Subtitle translation by: Jenny Kim

